# Cached API responses (~340MB) and derived CSVs. Both are reproducible:
# run scripts/run_all.py and they rebuild themselves.
#
# `data/processed/*` rather than `data/processed/` so git still descends into
# the directory and the two exceptions below can be re-included. With the
# trailing-slash form git never looks inside, and a `!` rule cannot rescue a
# file whose parent directory was excluded.
data/raw/
data/processed/*

# Two exceptions, because these are NOT caches that rebuild themselves:
#
#   club_research/  A dated snapshot of what beat writers, local press and
#                   podcasts said in the fortnight to 16 Aug 2026. Re-running
#                   the research next week gives different answers and after
#                   the season starts gives useless ones. It cannot be
#                   regenerated, only replaced.
#
#   injury_model.csv  Reproducible in principle, but only from a 244MB
#                   Transfermarkt scrape that is itself ignored and takes
#                   hours to rebuild behind a rate limit. 24KB is cheap
#                   insurance against that.
#   pro_rankings/   Published draft rankings from named analysts, gathered by
#                   web research and then re-fetched and checked row by row.
#                   The lists are dated and get taken down or overwritten; the
#                   research cannot be re-run to the same answer.
!data/processed/club_research/
!data/processed/injury_model.csv
!data/processed/pro_rankings/

# Virtualenv
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# API keys. This repo is public -- nothing with a credential in it goes in git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Anything produced after someone confirmed they wanted to break the league's
# no-AI-picks rule. See CLAUDE.md. Kept out of git because this repo is public
# and the rest of the league can read it.
output/cheat/

# The owner's personal draft rankings, if that workbook ever lands in here.
# It holds the actual pick order and must not be committed to a public repo.
*Arnav*.xlsx
*DrSN*.xlsx

# Excel lock files, left behind when a workbook is open
~$*.xlsx
.~lock.*#

# macOS
.DS_Store
